   "id": 667747,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"11\">\n    <li>Which equation is represented by the graph?</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p><img height=\"192\" src=\"exercises/media/10052d46a46cc19a.jpg\" alt=\"A graph of a downward-opening parabola on a Cartesian coordinate system. The parabola's vertex is at (4,4) and it intersects the x-axis at x=2 and x=6.\"></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1332043,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)=-{(x+4)}^2+4\">f(x)=-{(x+4)}^2+4</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1332044,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)=-{(x-4)}^2+4\">f(x)=-{(x-4)}^2+4</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1332045,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)={(x+4)}^2+4\">f(x)={(x+4)}^2+4</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1332046,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"f(x)={(x-4)}^2+4\">f(x)={(x-4)}^2+4</span>"
    }
